timeline
    title Non‑Cooperation Movement (1920‑1922)
    04 Sep 1920 : Launch of the Non‑Cooperation Movement by Mahatma Gandhi
    1920 : Nationwide boycott of foreign cloth, schools, courts, and legal services
    1920 : Alignment with the Khilafat Movement to unite Hindus and Muslims
    1921 : Congress session at Ahmedabad endorses non‑violent non‑cooperation
    1921 : Swadeshi enterprises promoted; Indian‑made goods encouraged
    Jan 1922 : Gandhi arrested and sentenced to six years imprisonment
    Feb 1922 : Chauri Chaura incident – violent clash leading Gandhi to call off the movement
    1922 : Formal withdrawal of the Non‑Cooperation Movement by the Indian National Congress